{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772726614,"nonce":"DZbh+v98JDGtstB/xtNHjpT436s=","title":"inbox ack: accept UUID prefix instead of requiring full UUID","message":"## Problem\n`mandible inbox ack auth_result \u003cid\u003e` requires the full UUID (e.g., `2181f239-0e4b-4dcd-ac8d-64a8c131a65e`). Passing a prefix like `2181f239` fails with \"item not found\". This wastes a tool call every time an agent uses the short form.\n\n## Proposed Solution\nIn the `inbox ack` handler, match the provided ID as a prefix against all inbox items of the given type. If exactly one matches, use it. If multiple match, error with \"ambiguous prefix: N matches.\" If none match, error as now.\n\nCollision probability: with \u003c 100 inbox items, an 8-char hex prefix (32 bits) has effectively zero collision risk.\n\n## Scope\n- Mandible CLI: `inbox ack` subcommand\n- Mandible API: `POST /api/inbox/ack` endpoint (if it does server-side matching)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e","files":null}]}